  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving the Control Capacity of DG Customs Enforcement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project targets improving the surveillance and control capacity of the customs in the movement of goods in the country specifically strengthening the customs control capacity in the areas of nuclear security and smuggling via parcel carriers. To this aim, 2 outputs are foreseen. Under Output 1 radiation control capacity of DG for Customs Enforcement will be improved through a draft situation report that will be prepared to identify the current situation and the gaps and needs related to radiation controls. In addition, two study visits will be organised to EU Member States for observing the best practices and benefit from lessons learnt in this area. A Customs Radiation Control Plan will also be developed through a collaborative process with relevant stakeholders. Under Output 2, mail and express courier control capacity will be improved. For this, ToTs and cascaded trainings will be delivered to government officials following the preparation of a Situation/Assessment Report for Mail and Express Courier Control. A study visit will be organised to an EU Member State to observe best practices and working modalities of the selected country through a combination of site visits, technical sessions and working meetings.</narrative>
  </description>
